This version reads `profile` and `profileIndex` into locals once. That lets the compiler keep them in registers instead of reloading the members. It also marks the valid-field path as the likely branch, so the common case falls straight through. The result is identical for every input:
- If `profile` is null or the index is out of range, it returns `FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID`.
- Otherwise it returns the field's `num`.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    const auto* p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect(p != NULL, 1))
    {
        const auto idx = profileIndex;
        if (__builtin_expect(idx < p->numFields, 1))
            return p->fields[idx].num;
    }
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```